{"title":"Do content creators need managers?","link":"https://www.usermag.co/p/do-content-creators-need-managers","date":1753281564000,"content":"<div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png\" width=\"1262\" height=\"776\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!YM6B!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0f2ae52a-bb76-4609-98d1-cff89ed64767_1262x776.png 1456w\" /><div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div></a><figcaption>Honarvar has made a name for himself building YouTubers into household names (credit: Garrett Lobaugh)</figcaption></figure></div><p>Zack Honarvar is one of the best managers in the content creator industry and for years, he has turned A list creators like Airrack into online behemoths. Now, he’s not so convinced YouTubers need managers.</p><p>Today he’s rebranding and repositioning his entire creator management company into an entertainment studio called <a href=\"http://www.itsgoodstory.com\">Good Story Studios</a>. “We want to be a creative partner with the creators that we work with,” Honarvar told me, “where, when they're coming up with ideas and we are packaging those ideas into materials and getting those into the hands of agencies and brands. [We also want to work more in] traditional entertainment mediums, like television, where we're pitching things as series.”</p><p>“I'm doing this because I don't believe creators should have managers and I'm trying to build the alternative solution,” he added. “I would always hear about creators having really bad experiences with management companies, and I started thinking through this problem of, what is the alternative, because I don't necessarily think every creator has the luxury of being able to hire their own internal teams. Many creators honestly don't want to hire and manage their own internal teams.”</p><p>Several popular creators have abandoned their managers in recent years. MrBeast parted ways with his management company last year, shortly becoming embroiled in scandal, in order to bring his business operations in house. Charli D’Amelio also took her business operations in house, hiring her agent Greg Goodfried away from UTA to become President of the D’Amelio media enterprise. Meanwhile, many management firms are taking a more active role in their clients businesses, acting more as creative partners than talent wranglers.  </p><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png\" width=\"572\" height=\"319\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!Ppre!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0cd2b3df-f4b9-4592-a347-899c8e7f138f_2246x1252.png 1456w\" /><div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div></a></figure></div><p>“We find that most creators have a media kit,” Honarvar said. “Then, their media kit gets sent out to a brand. Then, based on what their numbers are, a brand will say yes, read this 60 second integration in this video. What we're trying to do instead is think of a YouTube creator’s channel like a television network. What are the various series that they have within their channels where we can run a sales process as if it was a show?”</p><p>Good Story plans to be selective about who they partner with to start out.  They want to work with large creators who can build long-term IP and series. Unlike conventional managers who represent creators as talent and support every aspect of their business, Good Story will focus exclusively on sales and brand partnerships. “We want to [help creators] package ideas, pitch concepts, and build their vision from the ground up,” Honarvar said. </p><p>“YouTube is the future of TV,” Honarvar said. “More people are watching YouTube on their TVs than on their phones, and the content they’re watching is some of the most emotionally resonant storytelling happening anywhere.”</p><div><div><div><p>User Mag is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div><h2>Why we can’t stop doxxing people for fun</h2><p>Last week, a couple featured on the Jumbotron during a Coldplay concert in Boston <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CZUqGvOnLik\">went viral for being caught cheating</a>. Within minutes of the video spreading on TikTok and X, users rallied together to identify the couple in the video using AI and facial recognition tools. </p><p>Crowdsourced social media investigations are <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CZUqGvOnLik\">becoming more and more common</a>, and the people conducting them are leveraging increasingly dystopian surveillance tech that police and the feds are using against undocumented immigrants and marginalized groups. Meanwhile, all of our privacy is being eroded. </p><p>Jason Koebler from <a href=\"https://www.404media.co/\">404 Media</a> joined me to <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CZUqGvOnLik\">dig into the origins of the surveillance-entertainment economy</a>, how and why it evolved, and what we can do to protect ourselves. <a href=\"https://youtu.be/CZUqGvOnLik\">Watch here</a>.</p><div><div></div></div><div><div><div><p>User Mag is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, consider becoming a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png\" width=\"1407\" height=\"27\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 1456w\" loading=\"lazy\" /><div></div></div></a></figure></div><p><em>Sponsored post</em></p><p>As someone who reports on tech and privacy, I see how much personal data is just out there. Data brokers sell your name, address, phone number. And when someone buys your data, they see your whole family. Your spouse. Your kids. Your parents.</p><p>That’s why I use DeleteMe’s family plan. It removes my data and scrubs my relatives’ data too. It’s a powerful way to protect against identity theft, stalking, and harassment. I get reports showing exactly what they removed. If you care about keeping your family safe online, this should be standard.</p><p>Go to <strong><a href=\"http://JoinDeleteMe.com/Taylor20\">JoinDeleteMe.com/Taylor20</a></strong> and use code <strong>Taylor20</strong> for 20% off. Don’t just protect yourself, protect the people you love today. </p><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png\" width=\"1407\" height=\"27\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!4byi!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fad731c0e-8e05-47b8-abe6-56e409603eaf_1407x27.png 1456w\" loading=\"lazy\" /><div></div></div></a></figure></div><h2>What I’m reading </h2><p><strong>How Much Do Podcasters Really Earn? One Star Pulls Back the Curtain.</strong> </p><p>Joe Budden, a former rapper who now oversees a robust podcast network, gave a rare look into the finances of the industry. His network is on pace to generate $20 million in 2025. - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/bMQVb#selection-4309.0-4313.122\">NY Times</a></em></p><p><strong>The Website at the End of the Internet</strong> </p><p>Reddit is one of the last thriving islands of the old web. Can it survive AI? - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/E5vqI#selection-1203.0-1207.77\">NY Mag</a></em></p><p><strong>The Desperation of Donald Trump’s Posts</strong> </p><p>Trump’s social-media habits are different when he can’t control the narrative. - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/nj7t9\">The Atlantic</a></em></p><p><strong>The AI Industry Is Radicalizing</strong> </p><p>There are now two parallel AI universes, and most of us are left to occupy the gap between them. There have been disagreements between boosters and skeptics for as long as AI has existed. But in recent months, the argument has intensified as the industry aggressively expands across digital space. - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/KsA4j#selection-759.97-759.193\">The Atlantic</a></em></p><p><strong>Inside Silicon Valley’s strangest retreat, filled with taxidermy and smuggled treasures</strong></p><p>Call it the anti-\"Mountainhead\": A 23-acre complex of hooks, bones, and antique rifles is an unlikely hideaway for Palantir execs and AI founders. - <em><a href=\"https://sfstandard.com/2025/07/20/carmel-relic-collector-silicon-valley-retreat/\">SF Standard</a></em></p><p><strong>How a Video Studio Embraced A.I. and Stormed the Internet</strong> </p><p>The Dor Brothers are indie filmmakers whose viral videos are generated entirely by artificial intelligence. - <em><a href=\"https://archive.ph/WPEQ5#selection-463.0-467.107\">NY Times</a></em></p><p><strong>The intolerable memes of Alligator Alcatraz</strong> ﻿</p><p>The giddy, extremely online cruelty around the Florida detention facility reveals contempt for popular opinion. - <em><a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/policy/710015/alligator-alcatraz-ice-detention-memes-social-media\">The Verge</a></em></p><div><div><div><p>User Mag is a reader-supported publication. To receive new posts and support my work, become a free or paid subscriber.</p></div><div><div></div><div></div></div></div></div><h2>User Mag news rundown </h2><div></div><ul><li><p>There is currently <a href=\"https://x.com/helen/status/1947470973609165073?s=46\">a Labubu on Karl Marx's grave</a>.</p></li><li><p>Bari Weiss is <a href=\"https://www.ft.com/content/0f1ce3d6-35bc-461f-9685-13e2dfddb08d\">seeking a valuation</a> of between $200M and $250M for her right wing opinion outlet <em>The Free Press</em>.</p></li><li><p>The Bop House, the big OnlyFans content house, is <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DMbKSaPNjKN/?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D\">imploding over interpersonal drama</a>. One of the <a href=\"https://www.instagram.com/reel/DMbKSaPNjKN/?igsh=NTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D\">creators in the house breaks it down</a>.</p></li><li><p>Longevity enthusiast Bryan Johnson says he <a href=\"https://archive.ph/1iRe9#selection-1559.0-1570.0\">doesn't want to run his anti-aging company anymore</a>, says he wants to shut it down or sell it.</p></li><li><p>Silicon Valley AI startups are embracing China’s controversial ‘996’ work schedule, asking staff to commit to <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/story/silicon-valley-china-996-work-schedule/\">at least 72-hours per week</a>.</p></li><li><p>Google’s new AI shopping tool <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/technology/archive/2025/05/google-ai-shopping-tool-erotica-minors/682903/\">appears eager to give J. D. Vance breasts</a>.</p></li><li><p>Amazon just bought Bee, an AI wearable that <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/711621/amazon-bee-ai-wearable-acquisition\">listens to everything you say</a>.</p></li><li><p>NYC singles are l<a href=\"https://nypost.com/2025/07/22/lifestyle/sick-of-online-dating-nyc-singles-are-looking-for-love-via-powerpoint/\">ooking for love via PowerPoint</a> presentations.</p></li><li><p>Employers are <a href=\"https://sfstandard.com/2025/06/28/san-francisco-employers-are-hiring-etiquette-coaches-for-gen-z/\">hiring etiquette coaches for Gen Z</a>. Young workers need to be taught basic skills, from hygiene to eye contact.</p></li><li><p>Sam Altman is warning of an <a href=\"https://www.cnn.com/2025/07/22/tech/openai-sam-altman-fraud-crisis\">impending “fraud crisis”</a> because of how AI could enable bad actors to impersonate other people.</p></li><li><p>A DoJ staffer was fired after a decade at the agency in <a href=\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/us/news/2025/07/22/doj-employee-sacked-ice-app-husband/\">retribution for her husband’s anti-ICE app.</a></p></li><li><p>The AI platform Captions published a <a href=\"https://mirage.app/state-of-deepfakes-2025\">great rundown on The State of Deepfakes</a>.</p><ul><li><p>Very soon, most models will allow you to generate a person (real or synthetic) in any situation – without a duration constraint (longer than 12 seconds) and featuring multiple people in one shot.”</p></li></ul></li><li><p>Eater did an excellent rundown (with tons of photos) <a href=\"https://la.eater.com/scene-report/287082/tesla-diner-los-angeles-food-dishes-tech-design-review\">on the food at Elon Musk’s new Tesla diner</a>. </p></li><li><p>Teens <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/ai-companions-for-teens\">regularly chat with AI companions</a>, survey finds.</p></li><li><p>Are our dating standards getting too high? <a href=\"https://www.dazeddigital.com/life-culture/article/68290/1/are-our-dating-standards-getting-too-high-tiktok-bare-minimum-princess-treatment\">A new TikTok trend</a> has sparked discussions about what constitutes ‘the bare minimum’ in straight relationships.</p></li><li><p>A police department’s <a href=\"https://futurism.com/police-facial-recognition-random-arrest\">glitchy facial recognition tool</a> led them to arrest an innocent random man and accuse him of luring a 12 year.</p></li><li><p>AI-generated songs are showing up <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/spotify-ai-generated-songs-dead-artists-pages\">under deceased artists on Spotify</a>.</p></li><li><p>Everyone has agreed that 'Clanker' is <a href=\"https://mashable.com/article/new-robot-slur-clanker-trending-on-social-media\">the best slur for robots and AI agents</a>.</p></li><li><p>Leaked Slack messages show CEO of \"ethical AI\" startup Anthropic saying <a href=\"https://futurism.com/leaked-messages-ceo-anthropic-dictators\">it's okay to benefit dictators.</a></p></li><li><p>People on social media are <a href=\"https://archive.ph/Div8a\">obsessed with oversized bags</a>, aka BABs (Big Ass Bag).</p></li><li><p>The guy who <a href=\"https://www.thedailybeast.com/self-described-fascist-begs-for-donations-after-getting-fired-following-surrounded-debate-with-mehdi-hasan/\">proudly declared himself a fascist</a> in the latest Jubilee video claims he was fired from his job over it and has raked in thousands of dollars in donations.</p></li><li><p>Apple has <a href=\"https://x.com/AppleTV/status/1947733453341892904\">a new show from the creator of Breaking Bad</a>.</p></li><li><p>Apple launches AppleCare One, <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-07-23/apple-aapl-debuts-20-a-month-applecare-one-plan-covering-up-to-three-devices\">an insurance plan</a> covering up to three devices for $20 per month.</p></li><li><p>Uber tests the option to allow <a href=\"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2025-07-23/uber-tests-option-in-the-us-for-women-to-opt-for-a-female-driver\">women passengers to request</a> women drivers.</p></li><li><p>Google users are <a href=\"https://www.pewresearch.org/short-reads/2025/07/22/google-users-are-less-likely-to-click-on-links-when-an-ai-summary-appears-in-the-results/\">less likely to click on link</a>s when an AI summary appears in the results.</p></li><li><p>Democrats are desperately trying to <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/politics/711707/click-to-cancel-democrats-ftc\">revive the click-to-cancel rule</a>.</p></li><li><p>The AFP is begging the Israeli government to allow its freelance journalists to leave the Gaza Strip <a href=\"https://www.npr.org/2025/07/22/nx-s1-5476532/agence-france-presse-gaza-afp\">because they are starving to death</a> due to Israel’s food blockade. </p></li><li><p>Threads is <a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/news/711987/threads-is-trying-to-entice-creators-with-improved-analytics\">trying to entice creators</a> with better analytics.</p></li></ul><p><a href=\"https://www.usermag.co/p/do-content-creators-need-managers?utm_source=substack&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_content=share&amp;action=share&amp;token=eyJ1c2VyX2lkIjoxMTMxMTk5NywicG9zdF9pZCI6MTY5MDA2Njg5LCJpYXQiOjE3NTM3MzMzNzQsImV4cCI6MTc1NjMyNTM3NCwiaXNzIjoicHViLTMyMzgiLCJzdWIiOiJwb3N0LXJlYWN0aW9uIn0.ECpNFs2JiTyk5xIRvlU1X3mGwugDti9jYmMuKNPWH6U\"><span>Share</span></a></p><h2>Good posts</h2><div><figure><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://x.com/frogs4girls/status/1947768603555528850?s=10\"><div><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9S30!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bea8e3c-369e-41eb-a788-94274e356371_974x1058.png\" width=\"569\" height=\"618.0718685831622\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9S30!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bea8e3c-369e-41eb-a788-94274e356371_974x1058.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9S30!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bea8e3c-369e-41eb-a788-94274e356371_974x1058.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9S30!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bea8e3c-369e-41eb-a788-94274e356371_974x1058.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!9S30!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8bea8e3c-369e-41eb-a788-94274e356371_974x1058.png 1456w\" loading=\"lazy\" /><div></div></div></a></figure></div><div><figure>